    "title": "Giannis Antetokounmpo Discreetly Takes Next Big Step for Future By Purchasing $14M Property in City Speculated as His Next Basketball Home - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rolly Gacelo ,\n41 minutes ago New York Knicks are one of the teams said to have a better chance of landing Giannis Antetokounmpo and the Milwaukee Bucks’ latest financial move has people feeling curious.\nThe Greek Freak reportedly bought a property in Brooklyn . However, it is not for residence but more of an investment in real estate.\nJan 25, 2025; Inglewood, California, USA; Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) and coach Doc Rivers react against the LA Clippers in the first half at Intuit Dome. Mandatory Credit: Kirby Lee-Imagn Images The news was first seen on Reddit and people there were not jumping into conclusion right away about Antetokounmpo’s next move. The Bucks star’s future is heavily speculated amid the ongoing team struggle.\nX account TradedNY, which shares news about property purchases in the city, also posted about it and garnered reactions from NBA fans.\nApr 14, 2024; New York, New York, USA; Members of the New York Knicks hype squad launch tee shirts to the fans during a timeout in the third quarter against the Chicago Bulls at Madison Square Garden. Mandatory Credit: Wendell Cruz-USA TODAY Sports Giannis Antetokounmpo and New York Knicks Brooklyn is not NYC but since it is a property and not future Antetokounmpo residence, people still find ways to connect the dots.\nThe latest about Giannis and the Knicks says the interest from the team remains alive. However, things are about to get more complicated .\nOct 28, 2025; Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA; Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) reacts after scoring a basket in the 3rd quarter as New York Knicks guard Mikal Bridges (25) looks on at Fiserv Forum. Mandatory Credit: Benny Sieu-Imagn Images “If the Bucks are open to discussing Antetokounmpo with teams, the Knicks will no longer have the exclusive negotiating window as his preferred destination,” said NBA insider Shams Charania.\nThe only advantage they have right now is that they are reportedly Antetokounmpo’s preferred destination although he is not a fan of the city’s high tax rate. He is now a businessman though and the property purchase might say something.\nFor the latest Basketball Content Make sure you are always updated on your favorite basketball players and teams. Follow us @HardwoodHeroics for the latest and trending news about NBA, college basketball, and more. Stay updated by reading more of our NBA articles by clicking here and college basketball by clicking here !",
